  "interpretation_note": "This is a real-data test on the largest available TRGB catalogue (CF4, N = 285 usable with Vcmb > 200 km/s). It replaces the earlier register claim of an N = 350 differential sample that had no underlying data. A strong raw density-residual correlation is measured, but the distance-stratified Spearman rho changes sign across distance terciles and the density proxy is itself distance-correlated (magnitude-limited tracer field), so the gradient is dominated by the selection/flow confound rather than isolating a potential-depth lever. The matched Cepheid-TRGB subsample remains consistent with the Step-11 null. The claimed N = 350, 3.7-sigma, +0.039 mag gradient is NOT reproduced; the independent-kappa lever on the H0 ladder remains open."
